## Summary

| Location | Line(s) | What happens to `pendingInput` |
|---|---|---|
| `sendMessage` | 356 | **Sets** to `{ content, model }` when sending |
| `stream_complete` handler | 326 | **Clears** to `null` — the only normal-success path that clears it |
| `handlePreflightError` | 287 | **Replaces** with `{ userContent, "" }` for rollback |
| `loadSession` | 469 | **Clears** (via `createEmptyTabState()`) |
| `startNewConversation` | 525 | **Clears** (via `createEmptyTabState()`) |
| `sendNextQueued` | 691 | **Sets** to `{ content, model }` (same as `sendMessage`) |
| `retryLastMessage` | 392 | Does **not** touch `pendingInput` — it reads it and reuses it |

**Bottom line:** `pendingInput` is set when a message is sent (or queued for sending), and is cleared to `null` only on `stream_complete`. It is never cleared in `error` or `stream_aborted` handlers — in those cases, it may be preserved or replaced (e.g., `handlePreflightError` replaces it with the rolled-back content).
